argv: ["<ENV_ROOT>\\Scripts\\python.exe", "-m", "jev.check_baseline", "--help"]
usage: check_baseline.py [-h] --rows ROWS [--accepted ACCEPTED] [--out OUT]
                         [--expected-count EXPECTED_COUNT]
                         [--require-complete]

Compare archived-head decisions against the published accepted baseline,
offline. Supported row families are accepted predictions
(gold/pred/probabilities), archived replay rows
(status/gold/pred_old/n_options), and release head-route predictions
(options/independent_gold/choice/head_probabilities). They are never guessed
from a single shared field. Decode-route results are not archived-head
evidence. Every supplied row must be valid, unique and present in the accepted
baseline. Full accepted coverage is the default. For intentional smoke
subsets, --expected-count binds their size; --require-complete still requires
every accepted uid. This checks recorded decisions, not feature extraction,
live compatibility, or probability equality.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --rows ROWS           baseline, archived replay, or release head JSONL
  --accepted ACCEPTED   published baseline (digest checked); custom references
                        are marked unverified
  --out OUT
  --expected-count EXPECTED_COUNT
                        require exactly this many unique valid rows; permits
                        an explicit smoke subset
  --require-complete    require all accepted uids even with --expected-count
                        (default without it)
